# musician: a narrowed loadout for the hyoushigi OODA self-driver.
#
# A musician reuses the broad loadout only by *fork inheritance*; created fresh
# it lands here. The loadout governs the model's own tool calls and the kj verbs
# it runs through a shell tool: this one exposes no model-visible tools. It does
# not gate the tick. Every rc lifecycle, `tick` included, runs `kj` privileged
# (`ShellPolicy::Rc`), which bypasses the capability check, so the tick's
# `kj drive` runs whatever the binding says.
#
# A player's complete ABC text is prepared for the tick admitted by `kj drive`.
# The runtime validates notation; no model tool call is required. The `drive`
# grant below lets the context itself run `kj drive`, for example by hand.
set -e
kj binding allow "drive"
# Deliberately NOT granted: any builtin.* tool instance (block/file/resources/
# kernel_info/tool_search), facade:shell (the safe tool) or facade:shell_write
# (the hot one), facade:submit_input, and fork/drift/transport/operator/admin/house. A musician
# drives itself and emits ABC text; it does not call tools, fork, merge
# drift, run the transport, or do lifecycle.
